# Line endings.
#
# The repository already stores LF, and Prettier (which runs as an ESLint rule)
# expects LF. Without this file, a Windows clone with the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` checks every file out as CRLF, and `npm run lint` then
# fails with thousands of "Delete ␍" errors on files nobody edited.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working copy to LF on every platform, so the lint result is
# the same for everyone. This changes no committed content — only what git
# writes to disk on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
